# Source code for the OmniFile edge appliance {{RELEASE}}

The OmniFile edge appliance image {{RELEASE}} contains software licensed under the GNU General Public License
(versions 2 and 3), the GNU Lesser General Public License (versions 2.1 and 3) and other licences that require
the corresponding source code to be made available. Among them: the Linux kernel, Samba and winbind, parts of
systemd, GnuPG, NFS-Ganesha (with the OmniFile module FSAL_OMNI, LGPL-3.0) and the OmniFile Samba module
vfs_omnifile_prevver (GPL-3.0-or-later).

## Where the source is

The complete corresponding source for this release is published at no charge, in the public repository
<https://github.com/{{SOURCES_REPO}}>, as its GitHub Release **{{TAG}}**:

<https://github.com/{{SOURCES_REPO}}/releases/tag/{{TAG}}>

There is one release there for each appliance release. Download every `omnifile-edge-{{RELEASE}}-sources-*.tar`
archive and unpack them all into one folder (`ASSETS.SHA256SUMS` lists the archives' SHA-256). Together they hold:

- {{UBUNTU_SOURCES}} Ubuntu source packages (`ubuntu/`), exactly the versions in the image, as Ubuntu's archive
  had them on {{SNAPSHOT}} (`https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/{{SNAPSHOT}}/`, suites resolute,
  resolute-updates and resolute-security). `packages.tsv` maps every binary package in the image to its
  source package.
- `upstream/`: the Samba release the OmniFile Samba module is built in, with Samba's signature, and NFS-Ganesha
  and libntirpc at the exact commits the image's Ganesha is built from.
- `omnifile/`: the source of FSAL_OMNI (`fsal.tar.gz`, LGPL-3.0, including the scripts that build Ganesha with it)
  and of vfs_omnifile_prevver (`samba-vfs.tar.gz`, GPL-3.0-or-later, including its build script).

`MANIFEST.json`, `SHA256SUMS`, `packages.tsv` and this file are attached to the release on their own as well.
In the unpacked folder, `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` checks every file. About {{TOTAL_MB}} MB in all.

## Written offer

For at least three years from the date this release was first distributed, and for as long as we offer spare
parts or customer support for it, we will give anyone who asks a complete machine-readable copy of the
corresponding source code of the software in this image that is licensed under the GPL or LGPL, on a medium
customarily used for software interchange, for no more than our reasonable cost of physically performing the
distribution. To ask, open an issue at:

<https://github.com/{{SOURCES_REPO}}/issues>

{{CONTACT_EXTRA}}Name the release ({{RELEASE}}) in the request. The OmniFile components that are not under those
licences (the edge daemon and its tools, under the Business Source License 1.1) are not covered by this offer.

